{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics","id":1491187,"title":"Magical Prosthetics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-24T05:22:50-07:00","id":1491187,"title":"Magical Prosthetics","content":"For the purposes of this, assume Dissonance wasn't an issue and ignore the existence of Regeneration. <br /> <br /> How do you all envision magical prosthetics? Bionic arms intergrated with Wonderful Machine, or animated stone arms? Camera eyes, or flawless gem facsimiles? Pieces of Imbued jewelry that mimic the old functions, like an arm torc that casts Telekinesis to replace your missing forearm?<br /> <br /> I ask this for both an aesthetic preferences and novel solutions to disabilities. If you have any ideas I'd love to hear them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T06:40:53-07:00","id":1491194,"title":"","content":"Mind 3 Weaving; a glamour that makes everyone think you have an arm, nothing out of place. Actual function aside, you won\u2019t get any discriminatory/condescending attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T11:19:40-07:00","id":1491223,"title":"","content":"When designed with Forces and Matter, I see them as the ones in <i>Deus Ex: Mankind Divided</i>, just look up the individual <a href=\"https://deusex.fandom.com/wiki/Augmentations_(DXMD)\" target=\"_blank\">augmentation descriptions</a> to see what would be needed. Utilizing Forces to create high yield and endless batteries, creating nanotech polymers, using Perfected alloys to have room temperature superconductors and even using Weavings to make polymers with impossible properties. The biggest pains would be developing an interface for the central nervous system, creating a way to program them, dealing with rejection syndrome and preventing scar tissue buildup. But with the results would be mighty indeed.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cdnb.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/003/993/749/large/mathieu-latour-duhaime-adam-heart.jpg?1479267705\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Using <i>Zoom In</i> alongside clever use of Metter and Forces would allow the creation of nanobots, or even nano factories that stored specific blueprints (like Iron Man's armor). The advanced version would enable the real time regeneration of organs, while optimizing them using nanotech. Refer to the original <i>Deus Ex's </i><a href=\"https://deusex.fandom.com/wiki/Augmentations_(DX)\" target=\"_blank\">nano augmentation</a> descriptionsfor more details on how it works and what kind of augmentations can be installed. This would be, by far, the most discrete prosthetics.<br /> <br /> There are also combat prosthetics, which would essentially create up to <a href=\"https://battleangel.fandom.com/wiki/Zekka\" target=\"_blank\">a fully functioning body</a> for a mage who suffered catastrophic limb loss. Everything is fun and games until the android mage reveal they can shoot small amounts of antimatter they built in their miniature particle accelerator over a long period of time. These would require synthetic skin to function in Sleeper society, as well as something to dampen detection technology,<br /> <br /> Lastly, there could be full organic prosthetics, grown from scratch to match the person. Modified to look like everyday limbs via a chameleon function, but enhanced to suit the wearer. Artificial limbs that could act in emergencies where the user is unconscious, hands and hair that become <a href=\"https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Shaper_hand\" target=\"_blank\">surgical and medical tools the mage can employ</a>, skin that becomes a specialized exoskeleton (such fire and radiation resistance for those that suffered horrible wounds), legs that could use Van der Waals forces so someone who suffered in climbing accidents could scale as effortlessly as a gecko, and more. Since they are symbiotic living organisms, it means the integration process is probably easier, plus they can heal and develop on their own, which makes them more durable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-24-2022, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T13:03:01-07:00","id":1491233,"title":"","content":"Should the user have some way to hide the effects, then its possible a mage with Matter and Life could create a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JXAcAMtdowc\" target=\"_blank\">clockwork virus</a>. Why bother developing high end prosthetics when you can instead modify the subject to have a modular frame ? This would render them able to easily integrate replacement parts and weapons using commonly available hardware. Its especially advantageous because it could theoretically allow them to incorporate GM and Demon made Gadgets into the infected, which would make it a preferential way for the Austere and Pantechnicon to upgrade their favored Sleepwalkers and mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T14:41:25-07:00","id":1491241,"title":"","content":"It's a pity Telekinesis is a targeted spell. Combine it with Levitate and you could give someone with quadriplegia their mobility back.<br /> <br /> Ectoplasmic prosthetics seem like they'd be useful. Like really morbid playdough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:01:49-07:00","id":1491243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491241#post1491241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a pity Telekinesis is a targeted spell. Combine it with Levitate and you could give someone with quadriplegia their mobility back.<br /> <br /> Ectoplasmic prosthetics seem like they'd be useful. Like really morbid playdough.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if people who feel a lingering ghost limb are just sympathetically connected to its Twilight form ? So all they would need to do is use <i>Touch of the Geave</i> to pull it into the material. Another option is to use <i>Shadow Sculpting</i> to get limbs with a +2 bonus and that are more easily concealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:04:15-07:00","id":1491244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491243#post1491243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if people who feel a lingering ghost limb are just sympathetically connected to its Twilight form ? So all they would need to do is use <i>Touch of the Geave</i> to pull it into the material. Another option is to use <i>Shadow Sculpting</i> to get limbs with a +2 bonus and that are more easily concealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow Crafting? Sure, make yourself into the Ebon Dragon. Nothing can go wrong there :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:27:03-07:00","id":1491249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491194#post1491194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 3 Weaving; a glamour that makes everyone think you have an arm, nothing out of place. Actual function aside, you won\u2019t get any discriminatory/condescending attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another idea for a Subtly Arcane take of prosthetics: a Fate Weaving/Patterning spell to guarantee you always have a \u2018helping hand\u2019 i.e. someone willing to aid you, or a tool you can help yourself with. Reach to ensure their goodwill, have them perform better than usual, make them feel good about themselves, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:30:09-07:00","id":1491250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491249#post1491249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another idea for a Subtly Arcane take of prosthetics: a Fate Weaving/Patterning spell to guarantee you always have a \u2018helping hand\u2019 i.e. someone willing to aid you, or a tool you can help yourself with. Reach to ensure their goodwill, have them perform better than usual, make them feel good about themselves, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's both awesome and slightly horrifying. It's like subtle mind control. Indirect mind control? Either way, the ethics start getting a bit questionable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:33:20-07:00","id":1491252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491250#post1491250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's both awesome and slightly horrifying. It's like subtle mind control. Indirect mind control? Either way, the ethics start getting a bit questionable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still better than the Life mage next door who just chops off limbs from hapless victims to transplant them, Frankenstein style, immunities be damned <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:40:04-07:00","id":1491253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491252#post1491252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still better than the Life mage next door who just chops off limbs from hapless victims to transplant them, Frankenstein style, immunities be damned <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, Legacy powers don't twig Hubris, and that's totally the objective scale of morality! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Besides, that deer was going to be made into venison anyway. And the patient is much happier as a satyr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-24-2022, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T11:39:20-07:00","id":1491322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491194#post1491194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 3 Weaving; a glamour that makes everyone think you have an arm, nothing out of place. Actual function aside, you won\u2019t get any discriminatory/condescending attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure you can do that with veiling. You simple hide the absence of the arm from Minds, it will show up on security cameras though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T12:14:46-07:00","id":1491324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491322#post1491322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure you can do that with veiling. You simple hide the absence of the arm from Minds, it will show up on security cameras though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hide the absence, an interesting way to look at it, perhaps a Veiling of Death could be employed, since absence is within it's purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T14:30:46-07:00","id":1491348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491322#post1491322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure you can do that with veiling. You simple hide the absence of the arm from Minds, it will show up on security cameras though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically a very targeted version of Incognito Presence, so Veiling in Death or Mind should work. Forces illusions would probably be less ideal...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T00:24:06-07:00","id":1491398,"title":"","content":"Death has the advantage of working on things which aren't minds. But Mind makes people intentionally ignore it and like incognito presence (where you can walk through a crowded Street and people will not bump into you) they should go out of their way to avoid noticing it, like offering to shake your other hand even if they would normally try to shake that one...<br /> <br /> Veiling of Life should also work...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T01:15:24-07:00","id":1491401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491398#post1491398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Veiling of Life should also work...</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it? I'm sure I'm oversimplifying, but Life seems more like the &quot;blunt object&quot; approach to Veiling. You make everyone's instincts scream to ignore the non-arm, which isn't subtle. Incognito Presence (and the theoretical &quot;Death Shroud&quot;) at least plays on change blindness and &quot;not my problem&quot; blind spots.<br /> <br /> Edit: on the other hand, you probably could make something &quot;invisible&quot; to living organisms Ala Machine Invisibility...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-26-2022, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T03:20:54-07:00","id":1491409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491401#post1491401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it? I'm sure I'm oversimplifying, but Life seems more like the &amp;quot;blunt object&amp;quot; approach to Veiling. You make everyone's instincts scream to ignore the non-arm, which isn't subtle. Incognito Presence (and the theoretical &amp;quot;Death Shroud&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> at least plays on change blindness and &amp;quot;not my problem&amp;quot; blind spots.<br /> <br /> Edit: on the other hand, you probably could make something &amp;quot;invisible&amp;quot; to living organisms Ala Machine Invisibility...</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do two things with veiling, hide [purview] from everything or hide a thing from [purview].<br /> <br /> This would be hide the limb (purview of life) from everyone. Essentially using mutabke mask to &quot;alter her subject's apparent features&quot;.<br /> <br /> The downside of doing it with Life (compared to Mind) is that people will not make accomodations for the missing hand they think you have. <br /> <br /> Weaving with Life to transplant an actual arm might be more effective, perhaps combined with a veiling to look like your original arm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T03:48:08-07:00","id":1491412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491409#post1491409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaving with Life to transplant an actual arm might be more effective, perhaps combined with a veiling to look like your original arm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote up a Legacy based on that concept. It's very easy to turn it morbid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T08:34:08-07:00","id":1491768,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> I wrote a spell for this a while ago, I hope it inspires you.<br /> <br /> <b>Biomechanical Physiology (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> <br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> <br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Crafts, Occult<br /> <br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> <br /> For the spell's Duration, the target is both a living being and a technological device, which allows them to be affected with Crafts and Medicine interchangeably. Furthermore, the Mage has [Potency] points of bio-mechanical modifications he can apply to the target, which manifest upon a successful spellcasting rather than being installed manually. See the &quot;Transform Life&quot; and &quot;Wonderful Machine&quot; spells for examples of such modifications. Any supernatural attempt to undo or alter these modifications triggers a Clash Of Wills, using the highest between [Matter/Life]. Mundane attempts suffer a penalty equal to [Potency]. The Mage is limited to currently existing manifestations of biology and machinery.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach And 1 Mana: The Mage can give any sophisticated and fantastical modifications he can conceptualize.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach (1 Mana Optional): For the spell's Duration, the target is not restricted to their initial bio-mechanical modifications. Anyone (including the target themselves) can swap modifications for others through a Crafting Equipment roll of Intelligence + Medicine or Crafts. Each -1 imposed onto this roll takes 1 hour by default, and swaps out a modification for another. This requires access to suitable medical and mechanical equipment, unless the Mage also spends 1 Mana. In such a case, exchanging modifications can be done with one's hands alone and benefits from an effective Equipment Bonus equal to [Potency].<br /> <br /> +1 Reach or +2 Reach (1 Mana Optional): If the Mage spent +1 Reach and 1 Mana to allow the spell\u2019s subject to swap modifications using their own hands, this Reaching option allows them to shorten the interval to a single turn, in which they simply will their physiology into changing. With +2 Reach, this can be further shortened to a reflexive action if the subject of the spell suffers Lethal Damage equal to [Swapped Modifications], which is halved (rounded up) if the Crafting Equipment roll scored an Exceptional Success. With 1 Mana, the Damage from reflexive swapping is downgraded into Bashing.<br /> <br /> Add Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022: The bio-mechanical modifications may have properties and effects within the purview of the Forces Arcanum. This usually takes the form of cybernetic augmentations (e.g. optical fibers that can intercept and translate wireless signals, armored epidermis that transforms kinetic energy from enemy attacks into electrical energy for a ranged counterattack). This is limited to currently existing properties and effects, unless the Mage spends +1 Reach and 1 Mana to encompass any sophisticated and fantastical types he can conceptualize.<br /> <br /> Add Prime \u2022\u2022: The bio-mechanical modifications can incorporate Imbued Items with auxiliary and complementary effects. With Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, the Mage can not only make the Imbued Items himself, but adds the [Potency] of this spell to [Gnosis + Prime] to make these auxiliary and complementary Imbued Items. However, to benefit from this dice bonus, the Mana inside these Imbued Items must be in the form of Tass, and must have been gathered from a Hallow with a Technological Resonance. Each bio-mechanical modification can only be linked to a single Imbued Item.<br /> <br /> Add Death/Spirit/Mind \u2022\u2022: The bio-mechanical modifications affect the Ghostly, Spiritual and Goetic frequencies of Twilight, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-29-2022, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T08:52:50-07:00","id":1491769,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> Another cool option for magitech prosthetics is to replace limbs and organs with Fetishes, as per Spirit 4's &quot;Craft Fetish&quot; spell. You can replace your eyes with a Fetish containing Influence [Light 3] to let you see all sorts of unusual electromagnetic frequencies, for example. Just don't think too hard about the side-effects of cramming too many of those into your body, interlinking them, and then running out of Essence...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T13:51:54-07:00","id":1491812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491187-magical-prosthetics?p=1491769#post1491769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Another cool option for magitech prosthetics is to replace limbs and organs with Fetishes, as per Spirit 4's &amp;quot;Craft Fetish&amp;quot; spell. You can replace your eyes with a Fetish containing Influence [Light 3] to let you see all sorts of unusual electromagnetic frequencies, for example. Just don't think too hard about the side-effects of cramming too many of those into your body, interlinking them, and then running out of Essence...</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote up a Legacy to that effect. Imagine the abominations that could come from someone with Fetishes, Icons, and whatever magitech Vampires have, stuffed into them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}